=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_2d8e — Sunday friends: the living room becomes the social hub

Yuki and Omar are both home all day (weekend, no work). This Sunday, friends arrive in the evening, turning the two-person routine into a group social event. The dining table is set for a larger meal around 18:00; plates, glasses, and mugs are all in active use. After dinner the group migrates to the living room, and the room reconfigures: the snack bowl comes out of the cupboard and stays on the coffee table (it does NOT go back to the cupboard at 21:00 as it would on a weekday). The blanket is pulled onto the couch. The remote moves to the coffee table because it is being passed around. Multiple mugs and glasses are out simultaneously. The couch and armchair are occupied by guests, so the usual "Yuki settles in with one mug" pattern is replaced by a busier, multi-person setup.

What sets this apart from the weekday-evening documents: on a normal weekday the snack bowl goes to the cupboard at 21:00 (p_a3f7, p_c2f9, p_f1a6) and the remote stays at the TV stand (p_f1a6, p_a3f7). Here the snack bowl stays on the coffee table and the remote migrates to the coffee table. Only one mug is out on a weekday; here two or more are.

What would refute it: the snack bowl found in the cupboard at 21:00 on Sunday; the remote still at the TV stand at 21:00; only one mug in the living room at 20:00; the dining table empty of plates at 18:30.

No objects travel out of the house during this evening; both residents and their guests are in the home.

